2026-11-05  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	* ChangeLog: New, GNU style.
	* CLAUDE.md: New section ChangeLog (format, examples/ exempt); stage
	files by name.

	* lib/tcpsocket.js (TCPSocket.listen): The message callback no longer
	returns the result of dispatchEvent().  lws reads a non-zero return of
	a callback as "close the connection", so a server that wrote from its
	data handler lost the connection after the first message.

	* lib/serve.js (flush): Send a Date header and, for a body whose type
	is known, a default content-type, the way Bun does: text/plain;
	charset=utf-8 for a string, application/octet-stream for bytes, the
	type of a Blob, application/x-www-form-urlencoded for URLSearchParams.
	An in-memory string or byte body is now sent with content-length
	instead of streamed, so the connection can be kept alive.
	(Server#url, serve): Pass the iface 127.0.0.1 for the host name
	"localhost" (as Bun binds it); lws takes an interface name or an
	address, and with a host name listenPort stayed 0.
	* lib/lws/response.js (Response.json): Use "application/json;charset=utf-8".
	* lws-socket.c (lwsjs_headers_size): New.  Size of the header lines of
	a headers object.
	(lwsjs_socket_respond): Size the header buffer from the real headers
	(heap buffer when large) instead of a fixed 2 KB; a header that does
	not fit is an error and no longer dropped.  Chunked responses and the
	statuses 204, 304 and 1xx on h1 keep the connection alive (status line
	written without lws_add_http_common_headers, which answers
	"connection: close" for an unknown length).
	* tests/unittests/test-serve-bun-headers.js: New.
	* tests/unittests/test-large-response-headers.js: New.

	* lib/fetch.js (fetch): Retry once on a fresh connection when the
	request queued on the shared connection died with "server closed
	before responding", for bodies that can be sent again.
	(fetchOnce): New, the former body of fetch.
	(buildContext): Ask for 32 KB header buffers (maxHttpHeaderData).
	* tests/unittests/test-fetch-reuse.js: New.

	* lws-context.c (lwsjs_context_creation_info_fromobj): Read
	max_http_header_data.

	* lws-vhost.c (lwsjs_vhost_constructor): A callback mount that names a
	protocol which is not in the protocols list now throws a TypeError
	instead of creating a mount that never answers.
	* tests/unittests/test-vhost-bad-mount.js: New.

	* lws-socket.c (lwsjs_socket_write, lwsjs_socket_transaction_completed)
	(lwsjs_socket_long_poll_rxonly, lwsjs_socket_http_client_read)
	(lwsjs_socket_add_header, lwsjs_socket_client_http_multipart): Throw
	"socket is closed" when lwsjs_socket_destroy() has zeroed the wsi,
	instead of dereferencing a NULL pointer.

	* lws-protocol.c (lwsjs_callback_protocol): When wsi.close() is called
	from inside the ESTABLISHED or CLIENT_ESTABLISHED callback, run the JS
	closed handler ourselves, once: lws treats the connection as never
	opened and skips CLOSED, so onClosed() never ran.  The close code still
	goes out because the callback keeps returning -1.
	(pollfd_handler): Bound the forced-service loop to 64 rounds; the rest
	is picked up by the service tick, so a wsi that keeps asking for
	service can no longer starve JS timers.
	* lws-socket.h (LWSSocket): New bit closed_fired.
	* tests/unittests/test-ws.js: Passes now (no change to the file).

	* lib/websocket.js (WebSocket#send): The drain callback no longer
	returns the result of dispatchEvent().  lws closed the connection
	right after the first send().

	* lib/rpc/json-rpc-handler.js (handleSingleRequest): params is
	optional.  The message of a thrown error goes over the wire instead of
	"Server error", with the error's data or its name and message in data.

	* cmake/BuildLibwebsockets.cmake (build_libwebsockets): Pass the
	arguments after the legacy target name as step dependencies; the test
	"if(ARGN)" was never true inside a macro.
	* cmake/FindLibreSSL.cmake (find_libressl): Only query the libressl
	target when it exists; append LIBRARY_DIR to the install rpath, not
	the undefined LIBRARY_PATH.

	* tests/unittests/tinytest.js: TEST_ONLY=<substring> runs only the
	tests whose name contains it.  Print failures with console.log when
	console.error is missing (bare qjs).
	* tests/unittests/test-context-features.js: Pass the body before the
	headers to respond() (the other order sends an empty body) and resolve
	on the end of the HTTP transaction, not on the close of a kept-alive
	connection.
	* tests/unittests/test-udp-send-integration.js,
	tests/unittests/test-websocket-server-members.js,
	tests/unittests/test-websocket-static-methods.js: Import setTimeout,
	clearTimeout and exit instead of using the compat layer globals.
	* BUGS: Remove the fixed entries, file the new ones, note what could
	not be reproduced.

	* lib/logger.js, lib/lws/body.js, lib/rpc/common.js: A missing
	qjs-modules module (console, blob, bjson) is reported with a clear
	message.  (Written by another session; committed together with the
	serve changes above.)

2026-11-04  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	* lib/serve.js (serve): Translate the tls option with
	tlsContextOptions, forward the response headers, accept Uint8Array
	chunks of a streamed body, answer h2 bodies.
	(toResponse): Pass through a Response of another implementation.
	(respond): No error answer when the client has hung up.
	* lib/lws/response.js (wireData): New.
	(ServerResponse#flushHeaders): Send the first chunk together with the
	headers under h2.

	* lws-socket.c (lwsjs_socket_respond, lwsjs_socket_want_write): Throw
	"socket is closed" after the client disconnected; the wsi pointer had
	been zeroed by lwsjs_socket_destroy() and the native code crashed
	(segmentation fault in lws_add_http_header_status).
	* tests/unittests/test-server-client-disconnect.js: New.
	* tests/unittests/test-server-lifecycle.js: Import Response.
	* tests/unittests/test-tcpsocket-options.js: Use exit from std.

	* lib/tcpsocket.js, lib/lws/abort.js, lib/lws/streams.js: Import
	setTimeout and clearTimeout from os instead of relying on the global
	of the qjs-modules compat layer.

	* CMakeLists.txt: Install examples/chat-bridge/chat-bridge.js as
	bin/chat-bridge.  Run the unit tests with the bare qjs, with
	QUICKJS_MODULE_PATH set to the build and the module directories (not
	the source directory: a second module instance was loaded from it).
	* cmake/subst-lib-imports.cmake: Rewrite '../../lib/ imports of the
	installed script.
